    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_adbfbe52",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a Black man (Al Sharpton) pointing at a blurred portrait of Martin Luther King Jr., with text stating, 'if trump gets elected, i'm leaving the country!' and 'like and share if you think i should leave.' The overall intent is to provoke a reaction by using a figure associated with civil rights and social justice to express a political stance. The meme is harmful because it weaponizes the image of a revered civil rights leader to frame a political decision as a personal, existential choice, potentially undermining the legacy of MLK and reducing complex political discourse to a simplistic, emotionally charged statement. The juxtaposition of the serious historical figure with the absurdity of 'leaving the country' creates a tone of performative outrage that can be seen as disrespectful to the civil rights movement and its leaders. The meme also encourages engagement ('like and share') based on a potentially divisive political stance, which can amplify polarization and misinformation. While not overtly abusive or hateful toward a specific group, it is harmful by trivializing the gravity of political decisions and the historical context of civil rights leadership.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ab13f37b"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
